module test.claim.roadmap.worker_git_subtree_apply_spawn_wet_witness

// WORKER-ROOT-EQUIVALENT-3, THE EXECUTED HALF OF THE APPLY AND THE SPAWN.
//
// WHY THESE EXIST AND THE SHAPE CLAIMS DO NOT COVER THEM. The dry witnesses in
// test.claim.roadmap.worker_dedicated_account_witness decide on the model's ROWS -- which config keys the
// posture writes, which walks the migration runs, which paths the spawn grants. A row can name the right
// tool and still never run: an argv that is never executed reports the same tree as a step that was, so
// nothing in a shape claim can tell "the grant worked" from "the grant did nothing at all". So these
// witnesses call THE PRODUCTIONS -- dashboard_apply_provision_op's two git arms and
// belt_worker_git_entry_grant_readback -- and grade the result with git and with find, never with the
// builder that produced the state.
//
// THE PRINCIPAL, AND WHY NO NEW PRIVILEGE IS NEEDED. On the lab the apply reaches the instance as the
// instance's DIRECTORY OWNER (HostDashboardInstance.directory_owner -- the serve account, which owns .git and
// is a member of the attempt group; srv1 read, 2026-10-17), and the spawn's host steps run under the account
// the actuator runs as (HostExecArgv). These witnesses therefore run as whoever executes the claim and plant
// their throwaway .git with that account's own uid and primary gid -- the same relationship the lab has: a
// non-owner of the group reaching the tree only because the tree grants group write. NO NEW EXEC ROUTE: the
// apply's transport here is DashboardLocalProvision, whose realization is gunbc.WitnessBin.Run -- the route
// this file's sibling witnesses and the belt already run -- so driving the apply arms over a local instance
// IS executing them, not mocking them.
//
// WET: real processes, real trees, no network, no srv1, no GPU card, no systemd, no sudo. Excluded from the
// hermetic discovery corpus by this file's WitnessExclusionRow in gunbc.ci.ci_layer_roots, and enrolled
// function-by-function in v2.workflow.local_repo_wet_terminal local_repo_wet_schedule.
//   claim_batch --wet --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 \
//     --entry dag/test/claim/roadmap/worker_git_subtree_apply_spawn_wet_witness.dag --functions <csv>

